      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-heterolepis-and-a-microlepis/",
      "html": "<p>Acestrorhynchus heterolepis was scientifically described as early as 1878 by Cope from Peru. A. heterolepis has two dark horizontal bands, which is somewhat reminiscent of A. isalinae; however, A. heterolepis is unique in the genus due to a patch of scales of different size immediately behind the opercle. At that place A. microlepis has a small black blotch.</p><p>According to the scientific literature, both species can attain a maximum length of about 35 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/acestrorhynchus-heterolepis-and-a-microlepis/",
      "html": "<p>It is possible that the fish imported as A. microlepis belong to the species A. apurensis; A. apurensis and A. microlepis differ only in the length of the snout compared with the head length, and it is impossible to tell the two species apart without comparative material.</p>"
    }
  ],
